{"title":"2020 CMC 12B Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a convex quadrilateral such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a611329c69a958590b80104ccb58983c91625c95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=4, BC=4, CD=3, DA=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"276\" height=\"18\" />. There exists a unique point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> inside quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> such that the areas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/42657cfe16a4599d35e2dd1777717eb23a9cab34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAB, \\triangle PBC, \\triangle PCD, \\triangle PDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"261\" height=\"17\" /> are all numerically equal. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79c38ee17f61aa08c03a2b13afbd6ce45bedd57a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA^2+PB^2+PC^2+PD^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"210\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><ul><li>Step 1: Recognize the property**</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p>A known geometric result states:\n</p><p>&gt; If a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> inside a convex quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has equal areas of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abfbda2d3872e0896c549791425dec369ac52116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PAB, PBC, PCD, PDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"198\" height=\"18\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/590adc4d0b72f8b54445b421ba6f30108b491f4f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PA^2 + PB^2 + PC^2 + PD^2 = AB^2 + BC^2 + CD^2 + DA^2\\]\" width=\"446\" height=\"17\" />\nThis property allows us to compute the sum of squares of distances from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the vertices directly.\n</p>\n<ul><li><ul><li>Step 2: Compute the sum of squares of sides**</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p>We are given:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0a74de034d5b203d99a24f224fc3833283f31ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB = 4, \\quad BC = 4, \\quad CD = 3, \\quad DA = 7\\]\" width=\"323\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Compute the squares:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/f/a4fc646d28764189c32d6a9578f5c92eeb4a83c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB^2 = 4^2 = 16\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/59644cc2b3bae0b6c57d4860de2bd038fb5f1c83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BC^2 = 4^2 = 16\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b517c87afb4d80d09f572556d44430fc8d562219.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CD^2 = 3^2 = 9\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc4b5c256a22e44e5de46aed0bcbd9b23811ef80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DA^2 = 7^2 = 49\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Sum them up:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad7cdde7526a4a9543808bb93def51a5dd77e6d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB^2 + BC^2 + CD^2 + DA^2 = 16 + 16 + 9 + 49 = 90\\]\" width=\"408\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li><ul><li>Step 3: Conclude**</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p>By the geometric property of the equal-area point:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f2eb853fbefd40ac3a871796088a6e537d9c5f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PA^2 + PB^2 + PC^2 + PD^2 = 90\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li><ul><li>Answer:**</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f2eb853fbefd40ac3a871796088a6e537d9c5f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PA^2 + PB^2 + PC^2 + PD^2 = 90\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=~Trashboycan\" title=\"~Trashboycan\">~Trashboycan</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CMC_12B\" title=\"2020 CMC 12B\">2020 CMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2020 CMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 CMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"ex